7 3 3 7 5 3 7 7 3
15 8 8 8 15 5 8 1 15 5 8 15 15 15 8

[Editorial]
2056C - Палиндромные подпоследовательности Hints Hint 1 Analyze the example with $n = 6$. Hint 2 If $[a_1, a_2, \ldots, a_k, a_{n - k + 1}, a_{n - k + 2}, \ldots, a_n]$ is a palindrome, then $[a_1, a_2, \ldots, a_k, a_i, a_{n - k + 1}, a_{n - k + 2}, \ldots, a_n]$ is also a palindrome for all $k \lt i \lt n - k + 1$. Solution If $[a_1, a_2, \ldots, a_k, a_{n - k + 1}, a_{n - k + 2}, \ldots, a_n]$ is a palindrome, then $[a_1, a_2, \ldots, a_k, a_i, a_{n - k + 1}, a_{n - k + 2}, \ldots, a_n]$ is also a palindrome for all $k \lt i \lt n - k + 1$, because we make it's length odd and add $a_i$ to the middle. We can use this to create a sequence with a big value of $g$. However, we shouldn't create a palindrome of a greater length than $2k + 1$ by using the fact above. That make us try something like $a = [1, 2, 3, \ldots, n - 2, 1, 2]$. $f(a) = 3$ here, and any of $[a_1, a_i, a_{n - 1}]$ for $1 \lt i \lt n - 1$ and $[a_2, a_i, a_n]$ for $2 \lt i \lt n$ are palindromes, which means that $g(a) = 2(n - 3) = 2n - 6$. This construction works for $n \ge 7$, so we have to handle $n = 6$ separately. We can also use the construction from the example with $n = 6$ directly: $a = [1, 1, 2, 3, 4, \ldots, n - 3, 1, 2]$, which has $g(a) = 3n - 11$. Code

