From 24-hour format to 12-hour format, the minutes are the same. For the hours: If $\texttt{hh}$ is $00$, then it should become $12 \; \mathrm{AM}$. If $\texttt{hh}$ is from $01$ to $11$, then it should become $\texttt{hh} \; \mathrm{AM}$. If $\texttt{hh}$ is $12$, then it should become $12 \; \mathrm{PM}$. If $\texttt{hh}$ is from $13$ to $23$, then it should become $(\texttt{hh} - 12) \; \mathrm{PM}$. A fast way to implement this: replace the hours $h$ by $h \bmod 12$, and if this value is $0$, set it to $12$. Be careful to handle the case when $h$ and $m$ are single digits.

