is performed, we must have $a_1+a_3=a_2$. Then, rearranging the operations such that $op_1$ comes first will not impact the final result. Using the same line of reasoning, we can make $op_2$ the second operation, then $op_3$, and so on. To solve the problem, we can simply simulate the operations in this order, and then check if the array is sorted at the end. Time Complexity : $O(n)$ Code (C++) Rate The Problem! Heat Mid Horrendous Didn't Solve

