1985C - Good Prefixes Problem Credits: sum Analysis: cry Solution The only element that can be the sum of all other elements is the maximum element, since all elements are positive. Therefore, for each prefix $i$ from $1$ to $n$, check if $sum(a_1, a_2, ..., a_i) - max(a_1, a_2, ..., a_i) = max(a_1, a_2, ..., a_i)$. The sum and max of prefixes can be tracked with variables outside the loop. Code (C++)

