The first line contains an integer $t$ ($1 \leq t \leq 10^4$) — the number of test cases. The first line of each test case contains an integer $n$ ($1 \leq n \leq 2 \cdot 10^5$) — the length of $a$. The second line of each test case contains $n$ integers $a_1, a_2, \ldots, a_n$ ($0 \leq a_i \lt n$) — the elements of the array $a$. It is guaranteed that the sum of $n$ over all test cases does not exceed $2 \cdot 10^5$.

